es.dtypes.CategoricalDtype)\r\nOut[16]: \r\n0    a\r\n1    b\r\n2    c\r\n```\r\n\r\nI would think this either to work or either to raise an error that the dtype is not undertood.\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\n#### Code Sample\r\n\r\nWhen using dictionnary of dtype, it does not convert the dataframe :\r\nTypes are not modified whereas  df['col']= df['col].astype(type1)  works....\r\n```\r\ndtype0= {'brand': np.dtype('int64'),\r\n 'category': np.dtype('int64'),\r\n 'chain': np.dtype('int64'),\r\n 'company': np.dtype('int64'),\r\n 'date': np.dtype('O'),\r\n 'dept':  pandas.types.dtypes.CategoricalDtype,\r\n 'id': np.dtype('int64')}\r\ndf= df.astype(dtype0)\r\ndf.dtypes\r\n```\r\n#### Problem description\r\nWhen using dictionnary of dtype, it does not convert the dataframe :\r\nTypes are not modified whereas  df['col']= df['col].astype(type1)  works....\r\n\r\n#### Expected Output\r\ncolumns are converted into the desire types.\r\n\r\n#### Output of ``pd.show_versions()``\r\nPandas 0.19.2\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n# Paste the output here pd.show_versions() here\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"jreback","id":953992,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1Mzk5Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/953992?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback","html_url":"https://github.com/jreback","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_adm